ementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the reaper measures progress toward the 80% low-water mark (re-query footprint after each `docker rm`, or subtract each removed container's size) so the termination condition is deterministic and testable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'reaps oldest-first to an 80% low-water mark'","Observability section: 'from the SAME single docker system df call §2f already makes'","no stated per-iteration re-measurement protocol in the reaper description"],"finding":"AC-1 requires the reaper to reap to an '80% low-water mark', which requires re-measuring the writable footprint as containers are removed, but no section states whether the reaper re-reads the footprint per removal or estimates from a single initial reading. The observability section states the df call is made once for the heartbeat; the reaper's loop-termination measurement source is unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f34f926404d28cd88","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 1; 'What invokes the reaper' section","norm_id":"nde745203bf6bd6b3","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reaper removes one container, needs to decide whether the footprint is now under 80% — unclear if it re-queries the daemon or subtracts a cached per-container size"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a live/integration acceptance criterion that exercises the real docker daemon refusing `docker rm` (no -f) on a running container, or explicitly state how the daemon-enforced guarantee is validated without mocking that boundary.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'removal is docker rm WITHOUT -f, which the daemon refuses for a running one'","'candidates come from docker ps -a --filter status=exited --filter status=dead, which never lists a running container'","AC pins argv (never -f/-v/system prune) and name pattern, but no AC exercises a live dockerd refusing rm on a running container","'Portability: Docker APIs, systemd and local pytest only'"],"finding":"The reaper's core SAFETY guarantee is stated to be daemon-enforced ('removal is docker rm WITHOUT -f, which the daemon refuses for a running one'), but the acceptance criteria and test files are pytest-only. If docker is mocked in tests, the green suite asserts shell-level argv but never exercises the actual daemon refusal — the very guarantee the plan leans on to spare live backends is validated by proxy, not end-to-end.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc9363514b4d35aaa","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — '--reap removes nothing for ... a running row' / Safety section 'Two daemon-enforced guarantees, not shell logic'","norm_id":"nf63c14dde36b7a71","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pytest suite mocks docker ps/rm; the reaper safely computes candidates and issues rm, tests pass, but a real-world regression that passes -f (or a code path that force-removes) would not be caught because the daemon-refusal is never run against a live daemon"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: an integration test against a real (or dockerd-in-CI-less local) daemon that starts a running container, invokes --reap, and asserts the running container survives and rm returned the daemon's refusal — distinct from the mocked argv/pattern unit tests.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the rollback path (disable/remove the reaper timer, restore the 15 GiB image share) and note the effect of the reduced 13 GiB image cap on images already cached at cutover.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'images 13 GiB = 20 GiB, images having been 15 GiB'","'compose-up.sh (installs the timer)'","No stated rollback/undo step for the timer or the budget re-split; no statement of what happens to images already occupying >13 GiB at cutover"],"finding":"The plan re-splits the fixed 20 GiB Docker budget, cutting the image share from 15 GiB to 13 GiB, and installs a new reaper timer that changes runtime behavior of a deployed host, but states no rollback path or deploy-ordering for the change (e.g. what happens to already-cached images now over the reduced 13 GiB image cap, or how to disable the reaper timer if it misbehaves).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f09e276c4ee3779cc","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Which file owns what' (budget re-split 15->13 GiB) and 'What invokes the reaper' (new timer via compose-up.sh)","norm_id":"nbfb52821cd150152","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After deploy the image cap drops 2 GiB while the box already holds >13 GiB of images, triggering unexpected image prune pressure on the next tick with no stated revert"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a runbook line and AC covering timer removal and budget-revert, and state that the reaper/cap change is behavior-additive on a single host so the revert is `systemctl disable rebar-container-reaper.timer` plus restoring the share constant.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify what observability.sh --check-active inspects to set container_reaper_active (e.g. freshness of a reaper-written last-run stamp, not merely `systemctl is-active` or script presence) so a loaded-but-wedged/stale timer reads 0.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3767,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'container_reaper_active (1/0 heartbeat)' — no definition of the liveness signal","Plan: '§2i calls the side-effect-free --check-active' — the check's basis is unspecified","Plan: 'The second pre-empts the S4 finding: without it a silently-dead timer leaves usage nominal while nothing enforces anything' — the alarm's value depends on --check-active detecting a wedged/stale timer, not just a present script"],"finding":"The container_reaper_active heartbeat is produced by observability.sh --check-active (a process distinct from the reaper timer), but the plan does not specify what --check-active inspects to conclude the reaper is alive; if it merely checks `systemctl is-active rebar-container-reaper.timer` or that the script exists, a timer that is loaded-but-wedged (fires but the unit hangs, or last successful reap is stale) still reads active — the very S4 failure mode the rebar-container-reaper-not-active alarm claims to pre-empt.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0f5f462b9891d87a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan § 'What invokes the reaper, and what publishes the heartbeat' and § 'Alarms' (container_reaper_active / rebar-container-reaper-not-active)","norm_id":"n29d136599c2df3b9","priority":0.2233,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The rebar-container-reaper.timer is loaded and enabled but its last invocation hung or exited non-zero for hours; --check-active returns 1; the not-active alarm never fires while debris accumulates","The reaper script is present and the timer active, but the unit's TimeoutStartSec kills every run before it reaps; heartbeat stays green"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have the reaper write a timestamp/marker on each completed run and make --check-active emit 1 only when that stamp is fresh relative to the 5-min period (bounded like the other heartbeats), rather than probing timer/unit presence.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":